Subject: [PATCH] sun300iw1p1: initialize board PLLs in simpleboot, not FES

The simpleboot wrapper calls sunxi_board_init(), but the original
CFG_SUNXI_SIMPLEBOOT guard skips CPU PLL programming and the A27L2
clock source switch. The Falcon second stage jumps directly to OpenSBI
without initializing board PLLs, so flash boot can leave the CPU on
the BootROM clock source (HOSC, 40 MHz on this board).

Allow simpleboot to initialize the board PLLs and select CPU PLL for
A27L2. Keep this initialization disabled in FES, which returns to FEL;
the subsequently loaded simpleboot performs it. Preserve the PMBOOT
exclusion and correct the FES skip message.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/board/sun300iw1p1/clock.c b/board/sun300iw1p1/clock.c
--- a/board/sun300iw1p1/clock.c
+++ b/board/sun300iw1p1/clock.c
@@ -584,7 +584,11 @@ void sunxi_e907_clock_reset(void);
 
 void sunxi_board_pll_init(void)
 {
-#ifndef CFG_SUNXI_SIMPLEBOOT
+	/*
+	 * Simpleboot must program the PLLs and switch A27L2 to CPU PLL.
+	 * FES leaves this to simpleboot and returns to FEL first.
+	 */
+#ifndef CFG_SUNXI_FES
 #ifndef CFG_SUNXI_PMBOOT
 	printf("set pll start\n");
 #ifdef CFG_SUNXI_VF_2_1
@@ -645,8 +649,8 @@ void sunxi_board_pll_init(void)
 	set_pll_csi();
 #endif
 #else
-	printf("already init in simpleboot, skip\n");
-#endif /* pll already init in simpleboot */
+	printf("FES: defer board PLL init to simpleboot\n");
+#endif /* !CFG_SUNXI_FES */
 
 #ifdef CFG_GPADC_KEY
 	sunxi_gpadc_init();
